# Copy to .env and fill in. The server reads .env on start.

# The language model, NVIDIA Nemotron, behind an OpenAI-compatible API. It
# writes whispers, lookup cards, conversation filing, questions and long
# captions. Face matching works without it.
#
# Left empty, the server uses a vLLM server on this machine at
# http://127.0.0.1:8001/v1, which needs no key. ../README.md has the command
# that starts one. To use NVIDIA's hosted API instead, create a key at
# https://build.nvidia.com and set:
#   LLM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
#   LLM_API_KEY=<your key>
LLM_BASE_URL=
LLM_API_KEY=

# Optional.
# The model to ask for. With vLLM it must match --served-model-name.
# LLM_MODEL=nvidia/nemotron-3.5-lightning-30b-a3b
# HOST=0.0.0.0        # 127.0.0.1 keeps the server private to this machine
# PORT=8000
# DB_PATH=data/memory.db
